---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const LAST_UPDATED = "August 21, 2026";
const CONTACT_EMAIL = "hello@k-decoded.com";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms that govern your use of K-Decoded."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-brand-100 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-10">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-brand-700">K-Decoded</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-500">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

      <div class="prose prose-brand mt-9 max-w-none">
        <p>
          These terms govern your use of k-decoded.com (the "Site"), including its articles, vocabulary
          tools, and Community discussion feature. By using the Site, you agree to these terms. If you don't
          agree, please don't use the Site.
        </p>

        <h2>Who can use the Site</h2>
        <p>
          You must be at least 13 years old to create a Community account. If you're under the age of
          majority where you live, you should have a parent or guardian's permission.
        </p>

        <h2>Reading the Site</h2>
        <p>
          Articles, vocabulary lists, and flashcards are free to browse — no account required. Content is
          provided for general informational and educational purposes and reflects our own research,
          experience, and opinion at the time of writing. Prices, hours, event dates, and product
          availability can change after publication, so double-check anything time-sensitive before you rely
          on it.
        </p>

        <h2>Community accounts and content</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Sign-in:</strong> posting in the Community requires a passwordless email sign-in. You're responsible for keeping access to that email address secure.</li>
          <li><strong>Your content:</strong> you keep ownership of anything you post (topics, replies, images). By posting, you grant K-Decoded a non-exclusive, worldwide license to display, store, and distribute that content on the Site as part of operating the Community.</li>
          <li><strong>Your responsibility:</strong> you're responsible for what you post. Don't post anything you don't have the right to share, or anything that violates someone else's rights.</li>
          <li><strong>Guidelines:</strong> all Community activity is subject to our <a href="/community/guidelines">Community Guidelines</a>. We may hide, edit, lock, or remove content, and suspend or terminate accounts, that violate them.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Prohibited conduct</h2>
        <p>When using the Site, you agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Post unlawful, harassing, hateful, or sexually explicit content, or content that infringes someone else's intellectual property or privacy.</li>
          <li>Impersonate another person, post spam, or use the Community for unsolicited advertising or scams.</li>
          <li>Attempt to disrupt, scrape at scale, reverse-engineer, or gain unauthorized access to the Site or its underlying systems.</li>
          <li>Use the Site in any way that violates applicable law.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          Original articles, graphics, and site design are owned by K-Decoded unless otherwise credited. You
          may quote or link to our content with attribution; please don't republish full articles without
          permission. Product names, brand names, and images referenced in reviews belong to their respective
          owners and are used for identification and commentary purposes.
        </p>

        <h2>Affiliate links and advertising</h2>
        <p>
          Some posts contain affiliate links, and the Site displays ads through Google AdSense. See our
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for details on how that works and what data it involves.
          These arrangements never determine whether or how we review a product.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party links</h2>
        <p>
          The Site links to third-party sites (retailers, event pages, social media, other blogs) for
          reference. We don't control and aren't responsible for their content, accuracy, or practices.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The Site and its content are provided "as is," without warranties of any kind. We don't guarantee
          the Site will be error-free, uninterrupted, or that any information is complete or current.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, K-Decoded won't be liable for any indirect, incidental, or
          consequential damages arising from your use of the Site, including reliance on any information,
          product review, or user-posted content.
        </p>

        <h2>Termination</h2>
        <p>
          We may suspend or terminate your Community access at any time for conduct that violates these
          terms or our Community Guidelines.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms from time to time. If we make material changes, we'll update the "Last
          updated" date above. Continuing to use the Site after changes means you accept the updated terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact us</h2>
        <p>Questions about these terms? Reach us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
